READING
  The first failure is not 48+12=56; it is 48+8=56.
  The value 12 is a stable fold/parent count: it names U(5), R(4), source/sink deletion slices, and SC(6).
  The defect 8 is the first observer-extension/cut payload: node perspectives cannot see a rootless coupling, so the proof carrier must add incident words, edge-sector cross orientation, deletion fibers, and finally rectangle/hourglass residues when line-flow payload is attached.
  Controlled forgetting should therefore be stated as a payload law: a quotient is legal only when the forgotten coordinate is constant, reconstructed, dual-annihilated, descended to potentials, boundary-stopped, or routed to a named residual sidecar.
